<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  DROID_MODULE_BODYGROUP_WIRING_GAP_1. Found live-testing
  DROIDWORKS_MODULE_PERSONALITY_1: every Droidworks module apparel
  (Absorbed_KotorDroidModules_{Tech,Armor,Bases}.xml) requires one of
  RSW_DW_BG_ModuleHardware / RSW_DW_BG_ModuleSensor / RSW_DW_BG_ModuleSoftware
  in its <apparel><bodyPartGroups>, but nothing in this mod ever assigned
  those groups to a BodyPartRecord - every Droidworks race traces to
  DW_Race_Base, which uses the unmodified vanilla Human body
  (Races_Base.xml:50) - so no droid could wear ANY module. Live-confirmed:
  "success: true" on the wear debug action, but its own log said "has no
  body parts required to wear it", and jawa/pawn_get showed apparel stayed
  empty.

  Fix: add all three groups onto vanilla Human's own Waist BodyPartRecord -
  zero coverage, no organs, already exists purely to host the Belt apparel
  layer (see Human's own BodyDef). The three modules all use <layers><li>Belt</li>
  but each requires a DIFFERENT bodyPartGroup, so RimWorld's own
  ApparelUtility.CanWearTogether (conflict = shared group AND shared layer)
  lets a droid wear all three simultaneously - matching this mod's own design
  of three independent slots (hardware/software/sensor).

  Deliberately NOT a new BodyDef: Waist already carries zero coverage and
  no gameplay weight beyond hosting apparel, so adding these groups here
  costs nothing to any other Human-bodied pawn (nobody else has a module to
  put there) and needs no re-pointing of every Droidworks race's <race><body>.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/BodyDef[defName="Human"]/corePart/parts/li[def="Waist"]/groups</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>RSW_DW_BG_ModuleHardware</li>
      <li>RSW_DW_BG_ModuleSensor</li>
      <li>RSW_DW_BG_ModuleSoftware</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
